The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
strcat(volname, ".roclone");
strcat(volname, ".readonly");
```
Reason:
The use of `strcat` instead of `strlcat` for concatenating volume extensions can lead to buffer overflows and malformed volume names, as `strcat` does not check the size of the destination buffer, potentially exceeding its allocated length.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (strlcat(volname, tmpVolId?".roclone":".readonly", sizeof(volname)) >= sizeof(volname)) {
    code = ENOMEM;
    PrintError("Volume name is too long\n", code);
    goto fail;
}
```
Reason:
The replacement of `strcat` with `strlcat` ensures that the concatenation respects the size of the `volname` buffer, preventing buffer overflows and ensuring that volume names are correctly formed without exceeding the allocated space.

